WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
Local inference is frequently constrained by memory capacity and bandwidth.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:08.610
A full-precision language model may exceed the VRAM of a consumer GPU or the system RAM of

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.060
a small computer.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.710
Quantization reduces the weight footprint,

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:15.305
allowing a larger parameter count or more operating headroom on the same hardware.

00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:18.770
That headroom matters because the runtime, context cache, operating system,

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.085
and other applications also need memory.

00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:22.340
Fit changes performance.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.810
When a quantized model remains entirely on the GPU,

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.230
generation can avoid repeated transfers to slower system memory.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.245
On CPU-only systems,

00:00:29.245 --> 00:00:33.375
smaller weights reduce RAM demand and the amount of data moved through memory channels.

00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:36.915
Loading and startup can improve because fewer bytes are read from storage.

00:00:36.915 --> 00:00:39.680
These benefits vary with hardware and runtime;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.920
compact values still have to be unpacked and processed efficiently.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.640
Quantization expands practical choice, but it does not make every large model sensible.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.460
A heavily compressed model may fit while responding slowly,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.625
leaving little context headroom, or losing too much task quality.

00:00:52.625 --> 00:00:57.030
A smaller model at a healthier precision may be faster and more accurate for a specific

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:57.796
job.

00:00:57.796 --> 00:01:01.240
Capability depends on model design and training, not parameter count alone.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.640
Think in terms of a complete resource budget: weights, context, cache, batch, runtime,

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.775
and concurrent work.

00:01:06.775 --> 00:01:10.115
Select a quantization that fits with margin and test it on real prompts.

00:01:10.115 --> 00:01:13.240
The purpose is not to squeeze the largest possible file through startup.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.640
It is to make useful local AI responsive, stable, and affordable on available hardware.
